# Default config. Mount your own over /etc/tor/torrc to change anything.
#
# The hidden service directory is expected to be a mounted volume that either is empty (Tor
# mints a key and prints the new address) or already holds hs_ed25519_secret_key /
# hs_ed25519_public_key (the address you already own). Tor only ever rewrites `hostname`.
#
# Only DataDirectory is set on purpose: the state file and the cache live underneath it by
# default. Tor has renamed these options between releases (this config died on startup for a
# release over a "StatePath", which 0.4.9 does not know), so the fewer option names spelled
# out here, the less this image breaks when the base bumps.

DataDirectory /var/lib/tor/data

Log notice stdout

# Loopback SOCKS proxy: lets a sidecar (and `kubectl exec`) fetch the .onion through Tor
# itself, which is how a deployment gets verified end to end. Nothing outside the pod can
# reach it, and SocksPolicy rejects everything anyway.
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050
SocksPolicy reject *

HiddenServiceDir /var/lib/tor/hidden_service
HiddenServiceVersion 3
HiddenServicePort 80 127.0.0.1:8080
